" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-foot-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>20,000</span><span class="sb-foot-l" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>m² under one roof</span></div></div></div></section><!-- ═══ 2 · THE ROUTE — the page's one drawn module: a six-stop hazard axis ═══ --><section class="band g-clay" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>In transit</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>What Happens to a Parcel in Transit</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Every shipping box is bought for what happens between the packing bench and the customer's door. Six stages do almost all of the damage, and each one is a different kind of force.</p></div><ol class="sb-route" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><li class="sb-stop" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Pack Bench</h3><p class="sb-stop-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>0 in</p><p class="sb-stop-unit" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>drop height</p><p class="sb-stop-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Taped and sealed. Whatever is still loose inside travels on the first impact.</p></li><li class="sb-stop" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Line Haul</h3><p class="sb-stop-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>18 in</p><p class="sb-stop-unit" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>drop height</p><p class="sb-stop-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Floor to floor in a truck. Side walls bow and a loose flap catches the next pallet.</p></li><li class="sb-stop" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Sort Hub</h3><p class="sb-stop-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>22 in</p><p class="sb-stop-unit" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>drop height</p><p class="sb-stop-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Chutes, conveyors, and a scanner gate that turns away a label it cannot read.</p></li><li class="sb-stop" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Air Freight</h3><p class="sb-stop-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>24 in</p><p class="sb-stop-unit" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>drop height</p><p class="sb-stop-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The heaviest drop of the trip, in the driest air the carton will ever see.</p></li><li class="sb-stop" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Local Van</h3><p class="sb-stop-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>18 in</p><p class="sb-stop-unit" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>drop height</p><p class="sb-stop-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Loaded last, unloaded first. The most handling per mile travelled.</p></li><li class="sb-stop" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Doorstep</h3><p class="sb-stop-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>compression</p><p class="sb-stop-unit" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>the last hazard</p><p class="sb-stop-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Stored before it is opened. Compression, not impact, is what finishes this box.</p></li></ol><ul class="sb-reads" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><li class="sb-read" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><p class="sb-read-k" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>ISTA 3A Sequence</p><p class="sb-read-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>1 corner + 3 edge + 6 face</p><p class="sb-read-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Ten drops in a fixed order. The die is drawn against this sequence, and the run goes back through it before the print is locked.</p></li><li class="sb-read" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><p class="sb-read-k" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Two Kinds of Force</p><p class="sb-read-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>impact, then load</p><p class="sb-read-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Corners break while the parcel is moving; stacking and moisture finish the carton once it has stopped.</p></li><li class="sb-read" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><p class="sb-read-k" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>What the Route Sets</p><p class="sb-read-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>the corner post</p><p class="sb-read-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The hardest impact in the sequence decides the corner, and everything else on the board is read off that.</p></li></ul></div></section><!-- ═══ 3 · TYPES — six plates, two rows of three, three data pairs under each ═══ --><section class="band g-ivory" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Six builds</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Custom Shipping Box Types</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Six constructions cover almost every parcel. Each is chosen by what is inside and how many times it will be handled, not by how it looks on a screen.</p></div><div class="sb-types" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><article class="sb-type" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><figure class="sb-type-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/type-rsc.webp" alt="A plain kraft regular slotted container standing with its four outer flaps open" width="525" height="525" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-code" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>SB-01</span></figure><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Regular Slotted Container</h3><dl class="sb-spec" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>ECT</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>32–48</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Wall</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Single or double wall</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Closure</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Tape or glue</dd></div></dl><p class="sb-type-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The default: <b>four flaps and one die</b>, so a size change costs no new tooling, across the widest size range of the six.</p></article><article class="sb-type" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><figure class="sb-type-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/type-fol.webp" alt="A full overlap box held in two hands with its outer flaps covering the whole lid" width="525" height="525" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-code" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>SB-02</span></figure><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Full Overlap Box</h3><dl class="sb-spec" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>ECT</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>44–51</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Wall</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Double wall</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Closure</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Overlapped flaps</dd></div></dl><p class="sb-type-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Double thickness at the top and bottom, because <b>the outer flaps overlap a full width</b> where a load presses hardest.</p></article><article class="sb-type" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><figure class="sb-type-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/type-mailer.webp" alt="An open printed mailer box showing its printed inner liner and a moulded tray holding two bottles" width="525" height="525" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-code" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>SB-03</span></figure><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Die-Cut Mailer Box</h3><dl class="sb-spec" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>ECT</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>32–44</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Wall</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>E-flute</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Closure</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Roll end or tuck</dd></div></dl><p class="sb-type-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Folds into its own closure from a single piece, and <b>the inner liner is printed too</b>.</p></article><article class="sb-type" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><figure class="sb-type-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/type-telescoping.webp" alt="A two-piece telescoping box with its lid lifted clear of the base" width="525" height="525" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-code" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>SB-04</span></figure><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Telescoping Box</h3><dl class="sb-spec" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>ECT</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>44</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Wall</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Two-piece</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Closure</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Friction lid</dd></div></dl><p class="sb-type-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The lid slides over the base, so <b>the height is set after packing</b> rather than at the die.</p></article><article class="sb-type" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><figure class="sb-type-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/type-heavyduty.webp" alt="A large open double wall corrugated box standing on a paved outdoor surface" width="525" height="525" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-code" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>SB-05</span></figure><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Heavy-Duty Double-Wall Box</h3><dl class="sb-spec" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>ECT</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>48–51</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Wall</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Two flutes</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Closure</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Tape or strap</dd></div></dl><p class="sb-type-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Bonded from two flutes, so it carries a <b>stack four high or a single unit over 50 lb</b>.</p></article><article class="sb-type" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><figure class="sb-type-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/type-ecommerce.webp" alt="White printed shipping boxes shown with a lid open, carrying a placeholder brand mark" width="525" height="525" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-code" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>SB-06</span></figure><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>E-Commerce Shipping Box</h3><dl class="sb-spec" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>ECT</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>32–48</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Wall</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>E-flute</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Closure</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Self-lock</dd></div></dl><p class="sb-type-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Cut to the product footprint, with <b>the reveal printed inside</b>.</p></article></div></div></section><!-- ═══ 4 · THE VOID — the page's only cost arithmetic, and it is centred as a block ═══ --><section class="band g-clay" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd hd--c" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Dimensional weight</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>How Void Space Raises Your Freight Bill</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>A courier prices a parcel by the volume it occupies, not by the mass on the scale. A carton bought a size too large is paid for again on every order that follows, so the arithmetic is worth doing once.</p></div><div class="sb-void" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="sb-vrow" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Product, packed</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>6 × 4 × 3 in · 1.2 lb</span></div><div class="sb-vrow" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Box as ordered</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>9 × 7 × 5 in · 0.4 lb</span></div><div class="sb-vrow sb-vrow--calc" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Actual weight</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>1.6 lb</span></div><div class="sb-vrow sb-vrow--calc" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Dimensional weight (9 × 7 × 5 ÷ 139)</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>2.3 lb</span></div><div class="sb-vrow sb-vrow--calc" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Billed on</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>2.3 lb <b class="sb-air" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>0.7 lb of it is air</b></span></div><div class="sb-vrow" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Box cut to 7 × 5 × 4 in, same product</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>billed on 1.6 lb</span></div><div class="sb-vrow sb-vrow--out" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Billed weight removed</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>up to 25 %</span></div><div class="sb-vrow sb-vrow--total" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Label cost, against your own rate card</span><span class="sb-vval" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>10–25 % lower</span></div></div><p class="sb-void-note" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The re-cut is a change of die, not of box: same board, same print, drawn around the product as packed.</p></div></section><!-- ═══ 5 · TWO JOURNEYS — two cards, figure rows aligned to a shared baseline ═══ --><section class="band g-ivory" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Two journeys</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>How the Box Ships to You, and How It Ships to Your Customer</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>A shipping box is freighted twice and pays for both. The first journey is yours, and it is decided by whether the carton arrives formed or knocked down.</p></div><div class="sb-states" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><article class="sb-state" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Inbound — to your warehouse</h3><p class="sb-state-lead" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Knocked down and palletized, so freight is paid on board rather than on air. A formed carton on a pallet is mostly empty space; the same carton flat is almost all board.</p><dl class="sb-state-figs" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt class="sb-state-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>6×</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Units per pallet</b>Against the same carton shipped formed</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt class="sb-state-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>−83 %</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Freight volume</b>Per carton on the inbound leg</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt class="sb-state-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>+30 %</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Units per pallet, measured</b>Flat-pack optimization on a real run</dd></div></dl></article><article class="sb-state" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Outbound — to your customer</h3><p class="sb-state-lead" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Filled and sealed, then billed on the room it takes up. This is the leg where a box cut to the product and a box bought off a stock list stop costing the same.</p><dl class="sb-state-figs" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt class="sb-state-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>0.7 lb</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Air removed</b>On the void statement above</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt class="sb-state-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>1/16″</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Die tolerance</b>Held on every run</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt class="sb-state-v" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Volume</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>What the label is billed on</b>Not the weight at the counter, but the room the packed carton takes</dd></div></dl></article></div></div></section><!-- ═══ 6 · STACKING STRENGTH — the dark centre of gravity and the page's ONLY strength arithmetic ═══ --><section class="band band--dark g-dark" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd hd--light" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Board grade</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>How Stacking Strength Is Calculated</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Pick the grade from the height you actually stack to. Each figure is the load one carton carries on top of it with the safety and humidity allowances already taken out, so it can be read straight against the weight in your own racking.</p></div><ul class="sb-grades" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><li class="sb-grade" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="sb-grade-track" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-carton" style="height:52%" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>
