charge, so a short launch run still carries sharp detail.</dd></div><div class="sb-pair" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>CMYK and Pantone</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Matched against the brand reference and checked on the board itself, not against a screen.</dd></div><div class="sb-pair" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Inside print</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The reveal goes on the inner liner, letting the carton carry both the courier label and the opening moment.</dd></div></dl></div></div></section><!-- ═══ 8 · MATERIALS — the plate right, four compliance figures left ═══ --><section class="band g-ivory" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap sb-eco" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd hd--tight" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Materials</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Recycled and FSC-Certified Shipping Box Materials</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The most sustainable shipper arrives intact and gets reordered to the same specification. Each claim below is a figure a supplier can be held to, rather than a slogan.</p></div><dl class="sb-eco-figs" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="sb-eco-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>100 %</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Recyclable in a normal paper stream, tape and label aside.</dd></div><div class="sb-eco-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>FSC</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Chain-of-custody board on request, certificate number on the paperwork.</dd></div><div class="sb-eco-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Soy</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Plant-based inks, no mineral-oil carrier. The board recycles clean.</dd></div><div class="sb-eco-fig" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Plastic-free</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>No window film and no plastic tape needed to close the carton.</dd></div></dl></div><figure class="sb-eco-ph" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/materials.webp" alt="Plain kraft cartons arranged on a table with packing paper and botanical samples" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan></figure></div></section><!-- ═══ 9 · CASE STUDIES — image level with the copy, figures in a band beneath ═══ --><section class="band g-clay" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>From the floor</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Custom Shipping Box Case Studies</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Two orders where the carton was the whole problem, written up with the figures the plant recorded rather than the ones that read well.</p></div><div class="sb-cases" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><article class="sb-case" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="sb-case-body" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="sb-case-copy" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><p class="sb-case-tag" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Recycled corrugated · footwear</p><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Allbirds: A Primary Pack That Ships on Its Own</h3><p class="sb-case-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The brief was to move a footwear line to fully recycled corrugated without adding a second box around it. Early transit testing showed the recycled fibre giving way at the corners. The fix went into the flute geometry rather than into a thicker wall — re-cut and back through the drop sequence inside 48 hours.</p><a class="sb-case-link" href="https://www.leelinepackage.com/recycled-corrugated-packaging/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Read the recycled corrugated case study<svg class="btn-leaf" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></div><figure class="sb-case-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/case-allbirds.webp" alt="Flat-packed recycled corrugated cartons stacked on a wooden floor" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan></figure></div><dl class="sb-case-figs" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>7 %</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Lower total product emissions from the box design alone</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>48 h</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>To re-cut and re-test the flute geometry</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>0</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Secondary shipping boxes needed around the primary pack</dd></div></dl></article><article class="sb-case" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="sb-case-body" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="sb-case-copy" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><p class="sb-case-tag" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>E-flute to B-flute · kitchenware</p><h3 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Kitchenware: E-Flute to B-Flute Before the First Retail Order</h3><p class="sb-case-d" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>A crowdfunded kitchenware brand had a retail purchase order and a mailer that folded under a standard 50 lb drop test. The board moved to high-compression B-flute and the run was flat-packed. The barcode was re-laid on the new panel, and no pallet was turned away at the distribution centre.</p><a class="sb-case-link" href="https://www.leelinepackage.com/kitchenware-launch-case-study/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Read the kitchenware launch case study<svg class="btn-leaf" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></div><figure class="sb-case-ph" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/case-kitchen.webp" alt="A before-and-after pair showing a plain kickstarter mailer carton beside a retail-ready shelf display tray" width="900" height="490" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan></figure></div><dl class="sb-case-figs" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>&lt; 1 %</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Transit damage, from a mailer that crushed at 50 lb</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>+30 %</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Units per pallet after flat-pack optimization</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-6kutygan><dt data-astro-cid-6kutygan>100 %</dt><dd data-astro-cid-6kutygan>First-pass barcode reads at the retail DC</dd></div></dl></article></div></div></section><!-- ═══ 10 · REVIEWS — two cards, quote marks at the top-left and the bottom-right ═══ --><section class="band g-ivory" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Customers</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>What Our Customers Say</h2></div><div class="sb-quotes" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><figure class="sb-quote" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><blockquote data-astro-cid-6kutygan><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>We ship heavy, fragile glass bottles. Moving up to their custom-fitted inserts and 44 ECT double-wall shipping boxes completely eliminated our transit breakage rate, which used to hover around 4 %. The customer service team made the engineering process completely seamless.</p><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The order now runs to 12,000 cartons a quarter across two filling lines, and the board has come back identical on every reorder, which is what lets us keep one pallet pattern instead of re-drawing it each time.</p><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Damage claims fell from 61 in a year to nine, and the pattern they drew fits 14 more cartons on each truck.</p></blockquote><figcaption data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/avatar-david.webp" alt="Portrait of David L., supply chain manager at PureOrganics" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>David L.</b>Supply Chain Manager, PureOrganics</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="sb-quote" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><blockquote data-astro-cid-6kutygan><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Our e-commerce brand moved over to their custom white mailer boxes last year. The colors are incredibly rich, and the structural integrity is flawless. Our customers are constantly posting unboxing videos on TikTok, which has acted as free marketing for us.</p><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>The first order was 1,400 units; the most recent was 9,000. The unit price has come down at each step and the print has not moved.</p><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Returns for crushed corners are down from 47 a month to 11, and the inside panel is the thing customers photograph.</p></blockquote><figcaption data-astro-cid-6kutygan><img src="https://img.leelinepackage.com/shipping-box/avatar-sarah.webp" alt="Portrait of Sarah M., founder of Bloom Cosmetics" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span data-astro-cid-6kutygan><b data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Sarah M.</b>Founder, Bloom Cosmetics</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><!-- ═══ 11 · FAQ ═══ --><section class="band g-clay" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd hd--c" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Before you order</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="acc sb-faq" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><details data-reveal="up" open data-astro-cid-6kutygan><summary data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-faq-n" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>01</span>How do I know the board is strong enough for my product?</summary><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Send the packed weight and the stack height in your warehouse and the grade is quoted off the capacity chart in the section above, not off a stock size. If the stack is taller than the table allows, the board moves up rather than the answer being softened.</p></details><details data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><summary data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-faq-n" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>02</span>Does humidity change how high I can stack?</summary><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Yes, and it is the allowance most quotes leave out. Board loses compression capacity in damp air, so a stack that is safe on a dry floor is not safe in a stockroom that holds moisture for days. Every figure in that chart is the wet one.</p></details><details data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><summary data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-faq-n" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>03</span>Can you match a carton we already buy?</summary><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Send a flat sample or the existing dieline and the die is cut to it, holding the same ±1/16″ tolerance, and the new carton replaces the old without a change on the packing line. If the existing die has a weak corner we flag it before the run rather than after.</p></details><details data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><summary data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-faq-n" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>04</span>What is the minimum order, and how does volume pricing work?</summary><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>500 units per SKU. Between 500 and 1,999 units the rate drops 10–15 % off the standard rate, and above 2,000 units we quote per project. There is no die-cut charge and no setup fee added afterwards. The first quote is the whole number.</p></details><details data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><summary data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-faq-n" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>05</span>How long does a run take?</summary><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>A white dummy comes back in 3–5 days and a digital mockup in 24 hours, which checks the fit before anything is printed. Once artwork is approved, standard production runs 8–10 business days and a rush run 5–7. Tracking follows the job from press to loading dock.</p></details><details data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><summary data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="sb-faq-n" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>06</span>What artwork do you need, and can you print inside?</summary><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Vector files — .AI, .PDF, .EPS or .SVG. Where only a .PNG or .JPG exists, our artwork team re-draws it for print. Inside printing uses the same plate set, and putting the reveal on the inner liner adds a pass through the press rather than a second job.</p></details></div></div></section><!-- ═══ 12 · FINAL ═══ --><section class="band band--dark g-forest sb-final" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><div class="hd hd--c hd--light" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><span class="kicker" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Start here</span><h2 data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Start a Shipping Box Order</h2><p data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Two numbers are enough to begin: the packed size of the product and what it weighs. We return a dieline, a board grade and a billed weight.</p></div><p class="sb-final-cta" data-reveal="up" data-astro-cid-6kutygan><a class="btn btn-gold" href="/contact/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-astro-cid-6kutygan>Send the Packed Size and Weight<svg class="btn-leaf" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></p></div></section><footer class="footer" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><div class="footer-grid" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><div class="footer-brand" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a class="brand brand--light" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="LeelinePackage home" data-